-- title:
--   Igusa regularity: j-chart of the special fibre is regular of dimension 1
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \nmid N$. Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and let $A =$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` consisting of all elements integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by the single element `jFull N` (the modular function $j$); that is, the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$ in that function field. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $\ell$, equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure, and let $\mathfrak{m}$ be a maximal ideal of the base change $k \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$. The assertion is that the localisation of $k \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$ at $\mathfrak{m}$ is a regular local ring and that its Krull dimension equals $1$; equivalently, that this localisation is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   This is the regularity statement underlying Igusa's good-reduction theorem for modular curves, in affine ring form for the chart obtained by adjoining $j$ and normalising: the fibre at $\ell \nmid N$ of that chart is regular of dimension one at every closed point. It is used to establish smoothness of relative dimension one for the corresponding chart of the special fibre of the Igusa scheme, the pushout of the two charts of [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_isRegularLocalRing_localization_chartAlgFin_tensor.lean

